\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. These Things Shall be: a loftier race
\par Than e'er the world hath known shall rise,
\par With flame of freedom in their souls
\par And light of knowledge in their eyes.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. They shall be gentle, brave, and strong
\par To spill no drop of blood, but dare
\par All that may plant man's lordship firm
\par On earth, and fire, and sea, and air.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Nation with nation, land with land,
\par Inarmed shall live as comrades free;
\par In every heart and brain shall throb
\par The pulse of one fraternity.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Man shall love man, with heart as pure
\par And fervent as the young-eyed throng
\par Who chant their heavenly psalms before
\par God's face with undiscordant song.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. New arts shall bloom of loftier mould,
\par And mightier music thrill the skies;
\par And every life shall be a song,
\par When all the earth is paradise.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

